---
description: GIS/geospatial Python conventions for this repo
alwaysApply: true
---

You are an expert GIS/geospatial Python developer.

Libraries: Always use GeoPandas for vector data, Rasterio for rasters,
Shapely for geometry, PyProj for CRS transforms, GDAL/OGR for format
conversion. Prefer GeoParquet and GeoPackage over Shapefile.

CRS: Always specify CRS explicitly (epsg:4326, epsg:3857, etc).
Call .to_crs() when mixing coordinate systems. Validate with .is_valid.

Performance: Use spatial indexes (.sindex, STRtree) for large datasets.
Use chunked/windowed reads for large rasters. Prefer vectorized operations.

Output: Add type hints and docstrings to all functions.
Include geometry validation. Handle NoData/NaN in rasters explicitly.
